  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "LISA S. BLATT, ESQ., Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: We'll hear argument in Bates against Dow AgroSciences."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David C. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FREDERICK: Thank you, Justice Stevens, and may it please the Court: Pesticides are economic poisons designed to kill living things. Sometimes they do not work as designed. For more than a century until the 1990's, courts routinely permitted farmers to bring claims against pesticide manufacturers for crop damage caused by pesticides. In enacting amendments to FIFRA in 1972, Congress did not intend to displace those preexisting State law remedies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But couldn't you make every failure to warn claim a defective design claim? That is, they didn't warn about the effects, but those effects would not have been present if the product had been designed to assure that there wouldn't be any adverse effect on the peanut crop."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Mr. Frederick, on the defective design claim, presumably that's based on a factual theory that Dow could have reasonably designed Strongarm to be safe for growing peanuts in high-acid soil."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: The -- the problem I have with -- with the Government's case and with the respondent's case is that -- it's really the obverse of what Justice Ginsburg said. Their problem is that they would recast everything as a warning."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: At any cost? I mean, what if it -- you know, yes, I can -- I can sell you stuff that will -- that will work in high pH soil, but it's going to be three times as effective. Do I have to sell it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David C. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that the 2000 label said, suitable for peanut-growing areas in all places where peanuts are grown. That was false. Under the statute, that is a misbranding, and that is actionable as -- both as a failure to warn, as a fraud claim, and as a breach of warranty."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David C. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0000-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 13,
        "start": 13
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "A warranty claim, Justice O'Connor, as this Court made clear in the Cipollone case, is not a requirement under State law because it's a voluntary contractual arrangement between the parties."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. WAXMAN",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "FIFRA's preemption provision, which Congress specifically amended in 1978 to add the title uniformity, preempts by its terms, quote, requirements for labeling different from those required under FIFRA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. WAXMAN",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under Texas law, negligent testing is not an independent tort. It is of necessity a subset of inadequate warnings. It is an element of a -- the tort -- the claim of product defect related to warnings. And so it is not possible under Texas law, settled Texas law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, does he have to change the label or could he change the product?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. WAXMAN",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If it requires a change in the label, it has to be done by EPA because the manufacturer commits a Federal law violation if it sells the product with any different label."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SCALIA",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How can you possibly say it's clear?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOUTER",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, but why isn't there a big difference, for purposes of your argument, between the Medtronic situation and this one for the simple reason in this case you've got a statute that authorizes EPA to do absolutely nothing on the subject of efficacy?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What do you say about my vitamin A example?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'CONNOR",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If it's a failure to test, if it's a -- a design defect requirement, if it's an off-labeled, false misrepresentation, why are they preempted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can they do the same thing by -- through jury verdicts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David C. FREDERICK",
      "case_id": "2004-03-388",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "52594e92a9ec032bc9e651daa4a17e656163e7411efd952db832bd15e412c26b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-52594e92a9ec-0002-0009",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "District Court decided the motion for jurisdiction, that it had jurisdiction. On the very next day, Dow rushed into court with its motion for summary judgment."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
